      "writtenOn": "2023-05-16T22:23:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Even a `TAMPER_DETECT` file \"allows\" rollback/reset; it\u0027s just going to require the the client use a more permissive `ReadIntegrity` to read the file contents afterwards.\n\nMy intention was a rolled-back file  `TAMPER_DETECT_IGNORE_ROLLBACK` will _not_ return an error even if the client tries to read with `NO_TAMPER`. The filesystem storing the file might not even be able to detect rollbacks.",
      "parentUuid": "c0cd2e2e_67dcccdb",
      "revId": "4cf89cea4cd22a460d9d08cc21ed434c3092b63d",
