      "writtenOn": "2023-05-16T22:23:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, \"`TAMPER_PROOF` but non-persistent\" is something that keymint/keymaster want to use.\n\nAny of the `TAMPER_DETECT*` variants should make sense with either persistence value. After a wipe, any persistent files won\u0027t be modified and any non-persistent files will be reset. For any that are specifically `TAMPER_DETECT`, trying to read will be an error unless the client uses `ReadIntegrity.IGNORE_RESET`. For  `TAMPER_DETECT_IGNORE_*` files, clients will be able to read the reset file normally.",
      "parentUuid": "e50ea571_71eff24f",
      "revId": "4cf89cea4cd22a460d9d08cc21ed434c3092b63d",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
